WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.180
At rest, your heart beats about 60 to 100 times a minute.

2
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.540
Its muscle cells are crowded with tiny parts called mitochondria.

3
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.480
A white fat cell under your skin is different.

4
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.580
It is mostly one big drop of stored fat.

5
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.020
So what are the parts inside a cell?

6
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.960
And how do they work together to keep it alive?

7
00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.193
Many cells contain organelles.

8
00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:30.493
An organelle is a small part inside a cell that does a special job.

9
00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:33.633
The nucleus holds the cell's main instructions.

10
00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:37.393
The cell membrane is the thin boundary around the cell.

11
00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:39.833
It controls what enters and leaves.

12
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:46.047
The cytoplasm is everything inside the cell membrane except the nucleus: a

13
00:00:46.047 --> 00:00:48.387
jelly-like fluid and the organelles in it.

14
00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:52.687
The endoplasmic reticulum is a network of folded membranes.

15
00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.967
It helps make and move many proteins and fats.

16
00:00:56.987 --> 00:01:00.007
A vacuole is a sac that stores water, food and wastes.

17
00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.207
It is large in plant cells.

18
00:01:03.127 --> 00:01:05.767
Many animal cells have only small sacs instead.

19
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.210
Mitochondria release much of the energy stored in food.

20
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.390
One kind of food is the sugar called glucose.

21
00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.870
Mitochondria release that energy in a form the cell can use.

22
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.950
Metabolism means all the chemical reactions in the cell.

23
00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.030
Photosynthesis and cellular respiration are two examples.

24
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.303
The parts work together as one system.

25
00:01:30.663 --> 00:01:33.803
Instructions from the nucleus guide which proteins and fats are made.

26
00:01:34.643 --> 00:01:37.863
The endoplasmic reticulum makes and moves many of them.

27
00:01:38.963 --> 00:01:41.423
Mitochondria release the energy for this building.

28
00:01:42.223 --> 00:01:44.123
That building supports growth and repair.

29
00:01:45.103 --> 00:01:47.703
So trouble in one part slows many life processes.

30
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:50.357
Look again at the two cells.

31
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:56.517
Both have a nucleus, a cell membrane, cytoplasm, endoplasmic reticulum and

32
00:01:56.517 --> 00:01:59.337
mitochondria. The amounts are very different.

33
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.177
A heart muscle cell works without a break.

34
00:02:03.277 --> 00:02:05.077
Mitochondria fill a large share of it.

35
00:02:05.777 --> 00:02:07.257
A white fat cell stores fat.

36
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:09.757
One fat drop fills most of it.

37
00:02:10.477 --> 00:02:11.957
The other parts sit in a thin rim.

38
00:02:12.777 --> 00:02:16.057
So cells with different jobs hold different amounts of each part.

39
00:02:16.057 --> 00:02:18.737
Together, the parts keep the cell alive.
